		<div id="fsPageBodyWrapper" class="fsPageBodyWrapper">
			<div id="fsPageBody" class="fsStyleAutoclear fsPageBody">

				<main id="fsPageContent" class="fsPageContent">
							<h1 class="fsPageTitle">Board Election: November 2026</h1>




							<div class="fsPageLayout fsLayout fsTwoColumnWideLeftLayout fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_66031" data-use-new="true" >

				<div class=" fsDiv fsStyleTwoThirds fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_66032"  >

				<section class="fsElement fsContent" id="fsEl_66033" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_66033">Board of Trustees Election-November 2026</h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<p>Seats for Place 6 and Place 7&nbsp;will be on the November 3, 2026&nbsp;ballot. The seven Board of Trustees members are elected by all district residents and represent all district residents.</p>

<p>Candidate Filing begins Saturday, July 18, 2026 and ends at 5:00 PM on Monday, August 17, 2026. PfISD office are closed on the weekends so applications can be submitted in person starting Monday, July 20, 2026, at 8:00 AM. The last day to file a Declaration of Write-In Candidacy is Monday, August 17, 2026 at 5:00 PM.<br />
<a href="https://www.pfisd.net/fs/resource-manager/view/c234e452-f474-4713-a881-9f6df433eb1c">Notice of Deadline to File An Application for Place on the Ballot Cities, School Districts and Other Political Subdivisions</a></p>

<p>Interested candidates may file for a place on the ballot by submitting a completed and notarized Candidate Application; delivered in person, mailed through the US Postal Service or emailed.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>

<ul>
	<li aria-level="1"><strong>In-person:</strong> Applications may be submitted in person between 8:00 a.m. and 5:00 p.m. at the PfISD Administration Building located at 1401 W. Pecan St., Pflugerville, TX&nbsp; 78660, on days the building is open. Note: Hours of operation vary during the summer months. Please call 512-594-0000 to verify summer hours.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>

<ul>
	<li aria-level="1"><strong>By mail: </strong>PfISD Administration Bldg., Attn: Jacob Woolston, 1401 W. Pecan St., Pflugerville, TX&nbsp; 78660. Note:&nbsp;The Texas Secretary of State&rsquo;s Office requires the filing authority to be in possession of the application before the deadline. Applications postmarked before the deadline but not received by the deadline cannot be filed.</li>
	<li aria-level="1"><strong>By email:&nbsp;</strong>TO: <a href="mailto:jacob.woolston@pfisd.net">jacob.woolston@pfisd.net</a>, COPY: legal.services@pfisd.net</li>
</ul>

<p>For additional information, including the Candidate Packet, please see the <a href="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1QVa-45atSPjRmGHCzh7ZT9hKu-xirYWP">2026 BOT Election</a> information.&nbsp;</p>

<h3>Ballot Drawing</h3>

<p>If needed, a date and time will be set and communicated to all candidates as well as posted on the PfISD website.</p>

<h3>Eligibility and Filing for Candidacy</h3>

<p>To be eligible to be a candidate for, or elected or appointed to, the office of a school board member, a person must:</p>

<ol>
	<li aria-level="1">Be a United States citizen.</li>
	<li aria-level="1">Be 18 years of age or older on the first day of the term to be filled at the election or on the date of appointment, as applicable.</li>
	<li aria-level="1">Have not been determined by a final judgment of a court exercising probate jurisdiction to be totally mentally incapacitated or partially mentally incapacitated without the right to vote.</li>
	<li aria-level="1">Have not been finally convicted of a felony from which the person has not been pardoned or otherwise released from the resulting disabilities.</li>
	<li aria-level="1">Have resided continuously in the state for 12 months and in the territory from which the office is elected for six months immediately preceding the filing date.&nbsp;</li>
</ol>

<p>Applications filed are public records and can be reviewed upon request.</p>

<h3>Additional Information</h3>

<p><strong>Early Voting:</strong> October 19, 2026-October 30, 2026</p>

<ul>
	<li>Information regarding Polling Locations will be added when available from the counties.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Election Day: </strong>Tuesday, November 3, 2026</p>

<ul>
	<li aria-level="1">Information regarding Polling Locations will be added when available from the counties.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>

<p>After canvassing each election, the Board elects a president, vice president, and secretary to serve a one-year term. The&nbsp;Pflugerville ISD Board of Trustees consists of seven members. Board members shall be elected for three&ndash;year terms, with elections conducted annually.&nbsp;Board members are elected at large for specific places on the Board.</p>

<h3>Current Officers of the Board of Trustees</h3>

<ul>
	<li aria-level="1">President: Chevonne Lorigo-Johst</li>
	<li aria-level="1">Vice President: Kelly Daniel</li>
	<li aria-level="1">Secretary: Charlie Torres</li>
</ul>

<h3>Contact</h3>

<p><a href="mailto:jacob.woolston@pfisd.net">Jacob Woolston</a><br />
1401 W. Pecan St.<br />
Pflugerville, TX 78660<br />
512-594-0081</p>


	</div>


	</section>
	



	</div>
	
